{"tool_call": {"name": "set_schedule", "arguments": {"device_id": "thermostat_bedrooms", "schedule": {"daily": [{"time": "21:00-07:00", "temp": 65}, {"time": "07:00-21:00", "temp": 62}]}}}}

**💡 Lights** — Earlier evening schedule for shorter days:

{"tool_call": {"name": "set_schedule", "arguments": {"device_id": "lights_exterior", "schedule": {"daily": [{"on": "16:30", "off": "23:00"}]}}}}

{"tool_call": {"name": "set_schedule", "arguments": {"device_id": "lights_living", "schedule": {"daily": [{"on": "17:00", "off": "22:30"}]}}}}

**🔒 Locks** — Ensuring auto-lock is active:

{"tool_call": {"name": "set_device", "arguments": {"device_id": "front_door_lock", "state": "auto_lock_enabled", "parameters": {"lock_after_minutes": 5}}}}

✅ **All set! Here's your winter mode summary:**

| Setting | Configuration |
|---------|---------------|
| Main living areas | 69-70°F when home, 64°F when away, 62°F overnight |
| Bedrooms | 65°F for sleeping, 62°F during the day |
| Exterior lights | On at 4:30 PM, off at 11:00 PM |
| Interior lights | On at 5:00 PM, off at 10:30 PM |
| Front door | Auto-locks after 5 minutes |

This should keep you cozy while saving on heating costs when you're away or asleep. Let me know if anything feels off and I can fine-tune — for example, if 69°F feels too cool, or if you'd like the lights to come on at a different time. Enjoy the cozy season! ❄️

